librga (2.2.0-2+rkr7.20251126.79b3219) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * debian/control: give librga-dev the Depends it has never had upstream.
    Without it "apt install librga-dev" does not pull librga2, so the
    /usr/lib/*/librga.so the -dev package ships points at a library that is
    not installed, and anything linking -lrga fails with
    "librga not found using pkg-config". Anyone building against this
    archive hits it; ffmpeg's --enable-rkrga is the first consumer.
  * Same upstream commit as -1; this is a packaging-only change.

 -- Mixtile <dev@mixtile.com>  Tue, 08 Sep 2026 06:00:00 +0000

